{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeight_bounded_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeight_bounded_inv","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**Bounded degree gives a strictly decreasing coordination weight.** If the\ndegree is capped at `k` while `z` grows, `z·w` is pinned to the constant `ε·k`,\nso `w` falls like `1/z`. Stated as: two coordinations sharing one capped degree\nhave `z₁ · w₁ = z₂ · w₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeight_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeight_complete","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L135-L143","doc":"**The complete graph gives a constant coordination weight.** With `d = z`\nthe relation reads `z·w = ε·z`, so `w = ε` for every `z ≥ 1` — hence `Δw = 0`\nand `b₃ = 0`, recovering the pairwise wall from the degree picture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeightRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.coordWeightRel","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L130-L133","doc":"The coordination weight of a **degree-`d`** uniform-bond assembly, in the\nform `w z = ε·d/z` used in the module docstring. Stated as the defining\nrelation `z · w = ε · d` to stay in a ring without division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.not_uniform_simple_of_b3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.not_uniform_simple_of_b3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L118-L126","doc":"**The falsifiable form.** A measured `b₃ > 0` refutes the conjunction\n\"uniform bond weight\" ∧ \"simple graph\" — for *every* graph family at once, so no\nchoice of which pairs bind can rescue it.\n\nAME2020 gives `b₃ = +1.426220 MeV`, so the physical binding is not of this\nshape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_neg_of_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_neg_of_chain","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L109-L116","doc":"A chain on three vertices carries two bonds, and is strictly negative for a\npositive bond weight. This is the arrangement the canonical braid wires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_eq_zero_of_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_eq_zero_of_complete","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**The equality case is the complete triple.** `b₃ = 0` exactly when the\ntriple carries all three bonds and the pair carries one — the pairwise-additive\nassembly. Every sparser graph is strictly negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L89-L100","doc":"**The exclusion.** A simple graph on three vertices has at most three edges,\nand a bonded pair has at least one. Hence every uniform-bond simple-graph\nassembly has `b₃ ≤ 0`.\n\nNo monotonicity, no degree cap, no relation between mass numbers is assumed. The\nhypotheses are exactly \"the triple's graph is simple\" and \"the pair is bonded\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.b3Uniform","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UniformBondSimpleGraphExclusion.lean#L85-L87","doc":"The connected three-body cumulant of a **uniform-bond** assembly, written in\nterms of the edge counts alone: `b₃ = ε·(e₃ − 3·e₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}